1
00:00:10,560 --> 00:00:13,530
Give us a quick recap.
What happened in Phetchabun?

2
00:00:14,100 --> 00:00:16,960
The trip was full of cuteness, dude!

3
00:00:17,560 --> 00:00:18,640
I think...

4
00:00:18,660 --> 00:00:20,170
I'm gonna make a move on Jane.

5
00:00:20,950 --> 00:00:22,130
And do you think
he has feelings for you?

6
00:00:22,380 --> 00:00:23,470
How would I know?

7
00:00:23,750 --> 00:00:26,170
You two were alone together for two nights.

8
00:00:26,960 --> 00:00:28,440
Did you do anything that might have

9
00:00:29,170 --> 00:00:30,650
ignited the romance?

10
00:00:31,660 --> 00:00:33,050
Spending time with you

11
00:00:33,460 --> 00:00:35,600
makes my life seem a lot simpler.

12
00:00:36,260 --> 00:00:38,150
Stay with me for a long time, okay?

13
00:00:38,270 --> 00:00:39,350
Don't leave.

14
00:00:46,280 --> 00:00:47,470
Here you go.

15
00:00:48,160 --> 00:00:49,340
It's piping hot.

16
00:00:49,360 --> 00:00:51,600
Eat up. It'll make you feel better.

17
00:00:54,050 --> 00:00:55,170
Isn't it embarrassing,

18
00:00:55,360 --> 00:00:56,650
the state we're in?

19
00:00:58,640 --> 00:01:00,830
I don't think I drank that much last night.

20
00:01:01,080 --> 00:01:02,500
Why is my head hurting so badly?

21
00:01:04,350 --> 00:01:05,770
What the hell are you talking about?

22
00:01:06,360 --> 00:01:08,100
Your eyes were brimming with alcohol.

23
00:01:08,240 --> 00:01:09,560
Jeez...

24
00:01:09,760 --> 00:01:11,820
Your head was literally
inside a toilet bowl.

25
00:01:11,850 --> 00:01:13,100
And you're roasting me?

26
00:01:26,660 --> 00:01:27,940
A compensation

27
00:01:28,050 --> 00:01:29,800
for getting us into the car last night.

28
00:01:32,360 --> 00:01:33,770
It's totally fine.

29
00:01:34,040 --> 00:01:35,200
It was fun, actually.

30
00:01:40,800 --> 00:01:41,560
Hey!

31
00:01:42,620 --> 00:01:44,130
Am I missing out on something?

32
00:01:44,660 --> 00:01:45,470
Give me an update now!

33
00:01:45,740 --> 00:01:48,000
Well... It's nothing, actually.

34
00:01:50,470 --> 00:01:52,770
She's not talking about you.

35
00:01:54,270 --> 00:01:55,000
Really?

36
00:01:55,830 --> 00:01:57,470
Oh, okay. I'm sorry, then.

37
00:02:01,640 --> 00:02:02,770
That was close...

38
00:02:07,560 --> 00:02:09,530
You almost screwed yourself up.

39
00:02:10,200 --> 00:02:11,070
Just eat!

40
00:02:15,380 --> 00:02:16,300
Jaab, dig in already.

41
00:02:16,670 --> 00:02:17,860
Alright.

42
00:04:00,500 --> 00:04:03,370
[At what moment do we start
falling for someone?]

43
00:04:07,450 --> 00:04:11,730
"At what moment do we start
falling for someone?"

44
00:04:15,350 --> 00:04:16,700
This would be it!

45
00:04:18,170 --> 00:04:18,740
Huh!

46
00:04:20,270 --> 00:04:21,140
Jane!

47
00:04:21,650 --> 00:04:23,020
You're being rude!

48
00:04:23,040 --> 00:04:24,960
You're peeking at someone else's work.

49
00:04:25,750 --> 00:04:28,730
Khanoon said you're making
changes to the MV.

50
00:04:29,210 --> 00:04:30,840
But if this is rude,

51
00:04:30,860 --> 00:04:32,660
then I'll get back to doing nothing...

52
00:04:32,680 --> 00:04:34,250
Wait, Jane.

53
00:04:34,270 --> 00:04:36,930
Come on...
Don't be upset, you tiny boy.

54
00:04:37,740 --> 00:04:39,160
I'd like you, Mr. Jannarong,

55
00:04:39,180 --> 00:04:41,830
to offer me your assistance.

56
00:04:48,850 --> 00:04:50,530
Khanoon asked if I wanted noodles.

57
00:04:50,550 --> 00:04:51,460
Do you want some?

58
00:04:51,480 --> 00:04:52,730
The hot soup will sober you up.

59
00:04:53,950 --> 00:04:55,100
Um...

60
00:04:55,540 --> 00:04:56,540
I'm good.

61
00:04:56,560 --> 00:04:58,170
I had porridge already this morning.

62
00:04:58,190 --> 00:04:59,770
They're both soupy.

63
00:04:59,980 --> 00:05:01,650
I prefer something with rice.

64
00:05:12,410 --> 00:05:13,330
Jane.

65
00:05:14,480 --> 00:05:15,480
Well...

66
00:05:16,760 --> 00:05:19,570
I can't recall much from last night.

67
00:05:19,670 --> 00:05:21,530
Did I say something strange?

68
00:05:27,030 --> 00:05:28,200
You're asking me that again.

69
00:05:29,070 --> 00:05:30,800
You asked me the same thing
this morning.

70
00:05:33,170 --> 00:05:36,370
Do you usually do weird stuff
when you forget yourself?

71
00:05:37,360 --> 00:05:38,270
Uh...

72
00:05:38,860 --> 00:05:39,930
No, Jane.

73
00:05:39,950 --> 00:05:42,050
I just wanted to make sure.

74
00:05:42,070 --> 00:05:45,650
I don't want to act like a clown
and ruin this handsome look.

75
00:05:51,760 --> 00:05:53,650
Last night, I was also super drunk.

76
00:05:54,360 --> 00:05:57,400
I wasn't doing anything weird
around you, right?

77
00:05:58,970 --> 00:06:02,460
Have you ever...
loved someone?

78
00:06:03,550 --> 00:06:05,100
Have you ever been in a relationship?

79
00:06:06,270 --> 00:06:07,370
Jane...

80
00:06:07,970 --> 00:06:08,950
Why did you ask me that?

81
00:06:09,460 --> 00:06:11,070
When you feel that you...

82
00:06:11,610 --> 00:06:13,490
love someone

83
00:06:14,060 --> 00:06:16,040
who isn't your family,

84
00:06:16,060 --> 00:06:17,800
not a tree,

85
00:06:18,470 --> 00:06:19,860
not Auntie Kaew,

86
00:06:20,650 --> 00:06:22,050
what does it feel like?

87
00:06:22,930 --> 00:06:24,470
Are you...

88
00:06:25,360 --> 00:06:26,780
having...

89
00:06:26,800 --> 00:06:28,360
a crush on someone?

90
00:06:34,660 --> 00:06:36,000
You're quiet.

91
00:06:36,350 --> 00:06:37,070
I totally did.

92
00:06:37,350 --> 00:06:38,580
No... Jane.

93
00:06:38,600 --> 00:06:39,650
You didn't do anything!

94
00:06:40,340 --> 00:06:41,450
Tell me.

95
00:06:41,470 --> 00:06:44,130
Was I acting weird around you
without knowing?

96
00:06:45,070 --> 00:06:46,700
It wasn't weird, Jane.

97
00:06:47,060 --> 00:06:47,870
It wasn't.

98
00:06:48,120 --> 00:06:50,360
If it wasn't weird,
then what did I do?

99
00:06:50,730 --> 00:06:51,670
Well...

100
00:06:52,650 --> 00:06:53,650
You told me that...

101
00:06:54,200 --> 00:06:55,400
I...

102
00:06:59,150 --> 00:07:01,490
I don't remember much, Jane.

103
00:07:01,510 --> 00:07:02,270
Like I...

104
00:07:02,650 --> 00:07:04,670
I was also very drunk. Yeah.

105
00:07:10,460 --> 00:07:12,180
Are you sure that it was nothing?

106
00:07:12,460 --> 00:07:14,060
You didn't record anything, did you?

107
00:07:15,840 --> 00:07:17,350
I wish I had...

108
00:07:22,050 --> 00:07:23,000
- Jaab!
- Whoa!

109
00:07:23,140 --> 00:07:23,930
Spill it out!

110
00:07:24,070 --> 00:07:25,580
You didn't do anything, Jane.

111
00:07:26,070 --> 00:07:26,640
I swear.

112
00:07:26,770 --> 00:07:27,380
With...

113
00:07:27,900 --> 00:07:29,070
On my kitty cat's honor.

114
00:07:29,650 --> 00:07:30,370
I don't believe you!

115
00:07:30,390 --> 00:07:31,560
You didn't do anything, Jane.

116
00:07:31,580 --> 00:07:33,080
- I swear.
- Jane. Jaab.

117
00:07:33,640 --> 00:07:35,050
- What is it, Ai?
- Uh...

118
00:07:35,140 --> 00:07:39,280
Chomphoo sent me to tell you that
the meeting this afternoon is canceled.

119
00:07:39,300 --> 00:07:41,740
Bew hasn't gotten better,
so she can't make it here.

120
00:07:41,760 --> 00:07:42,600
Yes!

121
00:07:43,560 --> 00:07:45,030
That's what I'm talking about!

122
00:07:46,260 --> 00:07:47,800
Thank you, Ai.

123
00:07:47,870 --> 00:07:48,860
No problem.

124
00:07:52,050 --> 00:07:52,760
Hey.

125
00:07:53,340 --> 00:07:54,850
You're having so much fun
with these, huh?

126
00:07:56,770 --> 00:07:58,420
- There. Squishy.
- Ow, Jane!

127
00:07:58,440 --> 00:08:00,360
- Jane! It hurts!
- Squishy!

128
00:08:00,380 --> 00:08:01,760
Jane, it hurts!

129
00:08:16,930 --> 00:08:17,570
Whoa...

130
00:08:17,870 --> 00:08:18,480
Jane.

131
00:08:18,500 --> 00:08:19,260
Well...

132
00:08:19,560 --> 00:08:20,350
I...

133
00:08:20,890 --> 00:08:21,890
I'm hungry now.

134
00:08:22,550 --> 00:08:24,220
Can you help me pick my lunch?

135
00:08:24,240 --> 00:08:26,210
I... I can't come up with anything.

136
00:08:26,230 --> 00:08:28,890
Nothing soupy, though.

137
00:08:29,350 --> 00:08:30,490
Can you order
something for me, too?

138
00:08:31,960 --> 00:08:32,810
Huh?

139
00:08:34,040 --> 00:08:35,560
You didn't order noodles with Khanoon.

140
00:08:35,580 --> 00:08:37,120
I thought you brought your own lunch.

141
00:08:40,870 --> 00:08:42,860
Getting out of bed
was already hard enough.

142
00:08:43,560 --> 00:08:45,600
I didn't even have the energy
to press the microwave buttons.

143
00:08:48,260 --> 00:08:49,260
But...

144
00:08:49,750 --> 00:08:51,370
I don't want anything soupy either.

145
00:08:51,870 --> 00:08:53,150
If that's so...

146
00:08:53,170 --> 00:08:54,800
how about we eat out?

147
00:09:26,560 --> 00:09:27,270
Let's go, Jane.

148
00:10:12,870 --> 00:10:14,070
Whoa, Jane, Jane!

149
00:10:17,070 --> 00:10:17,960
Hey!

150
00:10:18,260 --> 00:10:19,260
You call that riding?!

151
00:10:29,870 --> 00:10:31,070
Why are you doing this?

152
00:10:31,860 --> 00:10:32,970
Why, Jane?

153
00:10:33,160 --> 00:10:34,600
I'm shielding you from the traffic.

154
00:10:36,320 --> 00:10:38,460
We're on the sidewalk.

155
00:10:38,760 --> 00:10:40,800
It doesn't matter.

156
00:10:40,950 --> 00:10:42,840
Why wouldn't it matter, Jane?

157
00:10:42,860 --> 00:10:43,610
The footpath is dangerous...

158
00:11:12,970 --> 00:11:14,500
Any side of the road is...

159
00:11:15,470 --> 00:11:18,000
just as dangerous.

160
00:11:18,570 --> 00:11:19,570
So please...

161
00:11:20,170 --> 00:11:22,870
live more carefully.

162
00:11:28,180 --> 00:11:29,000
Well...

163
00:11:29,360 --> 00:11:31,340
How am I not careful, Jane?

164
00:11:32,450 --> 00:11:33,250
Well...

165
00:11:33,450 --> 00:11:35,900
Eyes on the road.
Don't always look at me.

166
00:11:38,650 --> 00:11:40,970
And how did you know that
I was only looking at you?

167
00:11:41,500 --> 00:11:42,840
Or were you also...

168
00:11:42,950 --> 00:11:44,850
only looking at me?

169
00:11:45,650 --> 00:11:47,830
You're as tall as a durian tree.

170
00:11:48,060 --> 00:11:49,260
You're always in my sight.

171
00:11:50,350 --> 00:11:51,170
Huh!

172
00:11:51,740 --> 00:11:52,330
Whoa!

173
00:11:54,240 --> 00:11:56,950
Jane, that scared me.

174
00:11:56,970 --> 00:11:57,860
Give me a hug, please.

175
00:11:57,890 --> 00:11:58,740
Hey...

176
00:11:59,950 --> 00:12:01,400
- Come on. I'm hungry.
- Oh, Jane.

177
00:12:02,580 --> 00:12:03,530
Little bean sprout!

178
00:12:04,260 --> 00:12:05,700
Wait for this durian, please.

179
00:12:06,750 --> 00:12:07,840
Bean sprout!

180
00:12:18,060 --> 00:12:20,320
If others found out that
we're having lunch at a mall,

181
00:12:20,550 --> 00:12:22,540
wouldn't they be mad
that we didn't invite them?

182
00:12:23,400 --> 00:12:24,460
It's okay.

183
00:12:24,480 --> 00:12:26,210
They're eating noodles with Khanoon.

184
00:12:34,860 --> 00:12:35,860
And...

185
00:12:36,560 --> 00:12:38,080
Do you like Japanese food, Jane?

186
00:12:39,250 --> 00:12:40,250
It's fine.

187
00:12:45,960 --> 00:12:47,210
What do you like?

188
00:12:47,360 --> 00:12:49,550
Like, your favorite ones.

189
00:12:51,500 --> 00:12:52,700
Why are you asking me this?

190
00:12:53,960 --> 00:12:54,960
Well, I...

191
00:12:55,350 --> 00:12:56,530
I just want to know.

192
00:12:56,550 --> 00:12:57,670
Can't I?

193
00:13:00,660 --> 00:13:01,750
I'm not telling you.

194
00:13:02,050 --> 00:13:03,250
Or else you'll do
the same thing Min does.

195
00:13:05,400 --> 00:13:06,400
What do you mean?

196
00:13:09,730 --> 00:13:10,730
I don't know why,

197
00:13:11,150 --> 00:13:13,400
but everyone around me
likes to spoil me.

198
00:13:13,840 --> 00:13:15,650
I told Min about
my favorite food, right?

199
00:13:15,910 --> 00:13:17,530
And she just keeps treating me to it.

200
00:13:18,430 --> 00:13:21,070
She never picks the food she wants.

201
00:13:22,250 --> 00:13:23,020
Really...?

202
00:13:24,550 --> 00:13:25,670
Maybe it's because

203
00:13:25,870 --> 00:13:27,560
you're endearing?

204
00:13:28,350 --> 00:13:29,870
Endearing,

205
00:13:30,350 --> 00:13:31,670
adorable,

206
00:13:32,240 --> 00:13:33,240
and sweet.

207
00:13:34,230 --> 00:13:35,400
Something like that.

208
00:13:37,760 --> 00:13:39,550
And what's your favorite food?

209
00:13:40,850 --> 00:13:44,300
And... why are you asking me that?

210
00:13:44,860 --> 00:13:45,860
What?

211
00:13:45,880 --> 00:13:47,130
I want to know it first,

212
00:13:47,250 --> 00:13:49,130
so that I can spoil you later.

213
00:13:57,080 --> 00:14:00,260
And why do you want to spoil me?

214
00:14:08,440 --> 00:14:10,970
Alright. Let me get this for you.

215
00:14:11,070 --> 00:14:11,850
Here.

216
00:14:12,460 --> 00:14:13,460
It's really good.

217
00:14:13,850 --> 00:14:15,330
Try it.

218
00:14:29,610 --> 00:14:30,510
Jaab.

219
00:14:30,680 --> 00:14:31,510
Hm?

220
00:14:32,950 --> 00:14:34,600
After studying film,

221
00:14:35,050 --> 00:14:36,770
are movies less enjoyable for you?

222
00:14:39,040 --> 00:14:40,040
Way less.

223
00:14:40,960 --> 00:14:43,080
Back then, I only watched them
for fun, right?

224
00:14:43,100 --> 00:14:45,360
But after studying film,
I can't stop analyzing everything.

225
00:14:45,390 --> 00:14:47,170
The compositions and the emotions.

226
00:14:47,760 --> 00:14:49,200
It's like the theater itself is my classroom.

227
00:14:50,360 --> 00:14:51,750
It's the same for me.

228
00:14:52,150 --> 00:14:53,830
Studying film...

229
00:14:54,250 --> 00:14:55,560
makes me enjoy movies less.

230
00:14:56,660 --> 00:14:59,050
I can't even remember the last time
I went to a movie theater.

231
00:15:02,450 --> 00:15:03,930
I also...

232
00:15:03,950 --> 00:15:06,040
haven't gone to a theater
in such a long time.

233
00:15:06,570 --> 00:15:07,870
How about we...

234
00:15:08,270 --> 00:15:09,440
watch a movie together?

235
00:15:09,470 --> 00:15:10,860
But we have to get back to the office.

236
00:15:14,660 --> 00:15:15,370
Fine.

237
00:15:20,870 --> 00:15:23,480
Maybe next time.
Let's pick a date, too.

238
00:15:26,150 --> 00:15:27,150
Sure!

239
00:15:28,650 --> 00:15:29,960
You said it yourself.

240
00:15:30,470 --> 00:15:31,470
Mm.

241
00:15:32,900 --> 00:15:33,960
Okay.

242
00:15:34,220 --> 00:15:36,400
That's a promise.
You can't take it back now.

243
00:15:41,760 --> 00:15:43,270
Have you ever tried
those machines, Jaab?

244
00:15:44,250 --> 00:15:45,400
Of course, Jane.

245
00:15:45,470 --> 00:15:46,850
Everyone has tried them, no?

246
00:15:46,970 --> 00:15:48,140
Back in high school,

247
00:15:48,160 --> 00:15:50,960
I spent all of my allowance
on those things.

248
00:15:54,670 --> 00:15:56,200
Everyone but...

249
00:15:56,610 --> 00:15:59,790
this homeschooled country kid.

250
00:16:05,860 --> 00:16:06,960
Well, then...

251
00:16:07,360 --> 00:16:08,600
Wanna give it a try?

252
00:16:11,360 --> 00:16:13,040
Lunchtime is almost over.

253
00:16:13,060 --> 00:16:13,920
I don't want to be late.

254
00:16:14,050 --> 00:16:15,000
Hey...

255
00:16:15,080 --> 00:16:16,260
Trust me.

256
00:16:16,280 --> 00:16:17,120
It won't take long.

257
00:16:18,040 --> 00:16:19,440
Jane, let's do this!

258
00:16:21,220 --> 00:16:22,800
Come on, trust me. Let's go.

259
00:16:25,450 --> 00:16:26,450
Here, Jane.

260
00:16:26,650 --> 00:16:27,650
Give it a try.

261
00:16:31,160 --> 00:16:33,330
Aim for the center, okay?

262
00:16:33,350 --> 00:16:35,000
Three... Two...

263
00:16:35,020 --> 00:16:35,720
One! Go!

264
00:16:37,760 --> 00:16:38,510
Jane!

265
00:16:38,530 --> 00:16:40,530
Amazing, Jane! Let's go!

266
00:16:41,920 --> 00:16:43,250
Yeah, beautiful.

267
00:16:53,330 --> 00:16:54,650
Jane, wanna try?

268
00:16:54,670 --> 00:16:55,580
Come here.

269
00:16:56,140 --> 00:16:56,960
Come on.

270
00:16:56,980 --> 00:16:58,450
- I can't dance.
- Just give it a try.

271
00:16:58,470 --> 00:17:00,450
Don't be shy.
People will watch either way.

272
00:17:05,340 --> 00:17:07,720
Go, go, go.

273
00:17:07,860 --> 00:17:09,240
Spin, spin, spin.

274
00:17:09,660 --> 00:17:10,400
Go.

275
00:17:16,240 --> 00:17:17,440
Hit it. Hit it. Hit.

276
00:17:17,460 --> 00:17:19,120
Go, go, go.

277
00:17:20,790 --> 00:17:22,080
There. Hit there.

278
00:17:22,110 --> 00:17:23,360
Jane, Jane, Jane!

279
00:17:23,380 --> 00:17:24,470
This one. This.

280
00:17:25,090 --> 00:17:26,700
They're not popping up anymore.
Oh, there.

281
00:17:50,050 --> 00:17:50,880
Is it good?

282
00:17:51,660 --> 00:17:53,740
Wait, where are those two?

283
00:17:54,450 --> 00:17:55,450
Haven't seen them.

284
00:17:55,850 --> 00:17:56,560
Huh.

285
00:17:56,670 --> 00:17:57,840
Where are they?

286
00:17:57,870 --> 00:17:58,480
Huh?

287
00:18:00,160 --> 00:18:01,740
Maybe they're on a date?

288
00:18:03,510 --> 00:18:04,440
Seriously?

289
00:18:04,460 --> 00:18:05,480
I don't know.

290
00:18:09,680 --> 00:18:10,760
There they are.

291
00:18:10,780 --> 00:18:12,640
Speak of the devil.

292
00:18:12,660 --> 00:18:14,260
Ai, I brought you some treats.

293
00:18:14,540 --> 00:18:15,360
Thank you.

294
00:18:27,350 --> 00:18:28,260
- Hey.
- Hm?

295
00:18:28,280 --> 00:18:29,280
What are you two signaling?

296
00:18:29,760 --> 00:18:30,780
What do you mean?

297
00:18:30,800 --> 00:18:31,680
I wasn't doing anything.

298
00:18:31,700 --> 00:18:32,570
Nothing!

299
00:18:32,590 --> 00:18:33,840
You must be seeing things.

300
00:18:35,150 --> 00:18:36,630
I wasn't signaling anything.

301
00:18:36,650 --> 00:18:37,780
Nothing at all.

302
00:18:43,370 --> 00:18:45,360
The ride got canceled again.

303
00:18:48,750 --> 00:18:49,770
That's how it is, Jane.

304
00:18:49,790 --> 00:18:50,750
We're in the heart of the city.

305
00:18:50,780 --> 00:18:52,160
It's rush hour, too.

306
00:18:58,000 --> 00:18:59,320
I'm sleepy already...

307
00:19:05,860 --> 00:19:06,600
So...

308
00:19:06,860 --> 00:19:09,360
at what moment
do we start falling for someone?

309
00:19:09,570 --> 00:19:10,350
Huh?!

310
00:19:11,270 --> 00:19:12,270
Jane...

311
00:19:13,050 --> 00:19:14,280
What are you talking about?

312
00:19:15,360 --> 00:19:16,760
I'm talking about the MV.

313
00:19:17,350 --> 00:19:18,600
How about we come up with some ideas

314
00:19:19,300 --> 00:19:20,020
while we're waiting for our ride?

315
00:19:20,040 --> 00:19:21,220
So we won't waste time.

316
00:19:24,150 --> 00:19:25,560
Gosh, Jane.

317
00:19:25,580 --> 00:19:27,160
Next time, make it clear.

318
00:19:27,460 --> 00:19:28,460
Saying that out of the blue,

319
00:19:28,750 --> 00:19:30,280
you made my heart jump.

320
00:19:32,050 --> 00:19:34,160
You go first. I'll type it down.

321
00:19:34,970 --> 00:19:35,880
Well, then...

322
00:19:35,900 --> 00:19:37,320
How about we take turns?

323
00:19:37,340 --> 00:19:38,800
This way, we'll get various answers.

324
00:19:43,940 --> 00:19:45,480
Maybe it's the moment when the eyes meet.

325
00:19:56,340 --> 00:19:59,800
The moment when
someone cares about little details.

326
00:20:01,870 --> 00:20:03,600
They are fully themselves
when they're around each other.

327
00:20:04,140 --> 00:20:05,840
They feel at ease
whenever they're together.

328
00:20:06,740 --> 00:20:09,120
They feel like this person is the first one
to share stories with.

329
00:20:22,490 --> 00:20:23,750
The more they look at that person...

330
00:20:24,170 --> 00:20:25,440
the deeper they fall in love.

331
00:20:29,240 --> 00:20:32,080
The moment when they yearn
for that person all of a sudden.

332
00:20:33,440 --> 00:20:34,230
How's that?

333
00:20:44,670 --> 00:20:45,670
That works.

334
00:20:52,040 --> 00:20:53,340
What else?

335
00:20:57,480 --> 00:20:58,650
Well...

336
00:20:59,740 --> 00:21:00,960
The moment when...

337
00:21:03,670 --> 00:21:05,450
one is happy that their ride got canceled.

338
00:21:05,550 --> 00:21:07,760
- So the two of them will have more time...
- Hello?

339
00:21:08,040 --> 00:21:10,500
Oh, you can head inside the building.

340
00:21:11,470 --> 00:21:12,560
Okay.

341
00:21:15,210 --> 00:21:16,360
Jaab, we've got a ride.

342
00:21:18,140 --> 00:21:18,920
Really?

343
00:21:20,040 --> 00:21:21,040
Yay...

344
00:21:21,950 --> 00:21:23,570
Oh, by the way...

345
00:21:23,590 --> 00:21:25,720
what was the last one again?

346
00:21:26,960 --> 00:21:27,750
I...

347
00:21:28,140 --> 00:21:29,120
said...

348
00:21:29,470 --> 00:21:30,560
Hello?

349
00:21:31,940 --> 00:21:32,650
Okay. Sure.

350
00:21:32,670 --> 00:21:33,640
Just a moment, please.

351
00:21:34,150 --> 00:21:34,870
Jaab, our ride's here.

352
00:21:34,890 --> 00:21:35,580
Let's go.

353
00:21:40,280 --> 00:21:41,440
It's the moment...

354
00:21:42,050 --> 00:21:43,480
I get to be with you, Jane.

355
00:21:46,180 --> 00:21:47,280
Jaab, come on.

356
00:21:48,050 --> 00:21:49,050
Alright!

357
00:21:54,720 --> 00:21:58,520
[Jane]

358
00:22:28,960 --> 00:22:29,790
Oh...

359
00:22:30,370 --> 00:22:31,200
Jaab.

360
00:22:31,980 --> 00:22:33,800
Why are you so close to the screen?

361
00:22:35,830 --> 00:22:37,680
Why did you call me, kiddo?

362
00:22:40,160 --> 00:22:40,910
Whoa!

363
00:22:41,060 --> 00:22:42,680
You just got out of the shower, too?

364
00:22:44,950 --> 00:22:46,720
I was wondering about the last one.

365
00:22:47,480 --> 00:22:48,880
What do you mean? The last one?

366
00:22:49,050 --> 00:22:51,640
What we talked about
while we were waiting for the ride.

367
00:22:52,250 --> 00:22:54,680
I wasn't listening to your last example.

368
00:22:54,970 --> 00:22:56,560
I wanted to ask you in the car,
but I forgot.

369
00:22:57,050 --> 00:22:59,980
Oh, about that...

370
00:23:01,450 --> 00:23:03,050
Mm...

371
00:23:04,570 --> 00:23:05,600
I forgot.

372
00:23:05,870 --> 00:23:06,870
Completely forgot.

373
00:23:07,260 --> 00:23:08,520
I don't remember.

374
00:23:08,770 --> 00:23:09,770
Think harder.

375
00:23:12,870 --> 00:23:13,680
I...

376
00:23:14,170 --> 00:23:16,260
I forgot about it, Jane.

377
00:23:16,280 --> 00:23:18,250
Plus, for that MV,

378
00:23:18,270 --> 00:23:19,840
we only need a few examples.

379
00:23:19,860 --> 00:23:21,640
You already gave me plenty.

380
00:23:22,160 --> 00:23:23,360
Did I?

381
00:23:23,380 --> 00:23:25,960
I'll text them to you, okay?

382
00:23:26,130 --> 00:23:27,080
Mm.

383
00:23:29,000 --> 00:23:29,660
Oh.

384
00:23:30,530 --> 00:23:31,950
Are you telling the story in retrospect, Jaab?

385
00:23:32,230 --> 00:23:34,420
Oh, you mean the MV?

386
00:23:34,440 --> 00:23:35,280
Mm.

387
00:23:36,920 --> 00:23:39,360
You were looking for
the starting moments of a relationship

388
00:23:39,380 --> 00:23:40,760
for the end of the MV.

389
00:23:44,070 --> 00:23:45,270
Oh.

390
00:23:45,840 --> 00:23:46,640
Yeah.

391
00:23:47,170 --> 00:23:50,200
My goal is to include
good moments at the end.

392
00:23:50,480 --> 00:23:51,920
Good and sweet moments that...

393
00:23:52,270 --> 00:23:53,760
one cannot go back to

394
00:23:53,780 --> 00:23:55,720
no matter how much they miss them.

395
00:23:58,080 --> 00:23:59,080
I think...

396
00:23:59,560 --> 00:24:01,760
the vibe will be even sadder

397
00:24:01,780 --> 00:24:03,280
than the misunderstanding trope.

398
00:24:03,880 --> 00:24:04,920
That's what I think.

399
00:24:05,440 --> 00:24:07,360
You're such a mean director.

400
00:24:07,970 --> 00:24:09,880
You're not going to spare
the audience the pain?

401
00:24:09,900 --> 00:24:11,040
Come on, Jane.

402
00:24:11,060 --> 00:24:12,620
It has to feel realistic, alright?

403
00:24:12,640 --> 00:24:13,650
It has to make them...

404
00:24:14,800 --> 00:24:17,440
cry their eyes out.

405
00:24:18,800 --> 00:24:20,320
Like, "Why is it so sad?"

406
00:24:20,570 --> 00:24:21,440
Something like that.

407
00:24:26,150 --> 00:24:27,280
Have you put on the blanket?

408
00:24:32,640 --> 00:24:33,400
Mm.

409
00:24:33,740 --> 00:24:34,600
Yes.

410
00:24:35,250 --> 00:24:35,960
Mm.

411
00:24:36,270 --> 00:24:37,400
You should go to bed, then.

412
00:24:38,150 --> 00:24:39,660
I'm already in bed.

413
00:24:40,160 --> 00:24:41,320
That's not what I meant.

414
00:24:41,560 --> 00:24:42,920
I mean, you should...

415
00:24:45,660 --> 00:24:46,600
Like this.

416
00:24:49,040 --> 00:24:49,960
I'm hanging up, okay?

417
00:24:50,670 --> 00:24:51,520
Mm.

418
00:24:51,870 --> 00:24:53,060
See you tomorrow.

419
00:24:53,720 --> 00:24:54,560
Sweet dreams.

420
00:24:55,770 --> 00:24:56,770
Good night.

421
00:25:13,200 --> 00:25:16,440
[The 66 Cottage]

422
00:25:27,120 --> 00:25:28,360
What would you like, Jane?

423
00:25:28,520 --> 00:25:31,000
Almond milk latte with no sugar?
The usual?

424
00:25:31,630 --> 00:25:32,230
Right.

425
00:25:47,030 --> 00:25:49,750
Almond milk latte with no sugar?

426
00:25:50,730 --> 00:25:51,730
Oh...

427
00:25:52,040 --> 00:25:53,450
Oh, yes...

428
00:25:53,470 --> 00:25:56,630
And I'll have a cup of black coffee, please.

429
00:25:57,450 --> 00:25:58,920
Also no sugar.

430
00:25:59,280 --> 00:26:00,200
Alright.

431
00:26:02,570 --> 00:26:05,900
In case you're interested,
we have a weekend promotion.

432
00:26:05,920 --> 00:26:09,740
You can write wishes and messages
on postcards.

433
00:26:09,770 --> 00:26:13,140
They'll be displayed in the shop
as a thank you to our first group of customers.

434
00:26:13,160 --> 00:26:14,610
Whoa...

435
00:26:14,630 --> 00:26:16,020
That's like...

436
00:26:16,130 --> 00:26:18,660
writing our names on
temple roof tiles for merits.

437
00:26:18,680 --> 00:26:19,400
Yeah?

438
00:26:19,480 --> 00:26:20,010
Ow!

439
00:26:21,440 --> 00:26:22,340
Uh...

440
00:26:22,360 --> 00:26:23,790
That's such a lovely idea.

441
00:26:24,230 --> 00:26:25,730
I'll also have that one, please.

442
00:26:25,750 --> 00:26:26,750
Alright.

443
00:26:27,440 --> 00:26:29,030
We'll bring your order to your table.

444
00:26:29,050 --> 00:26:29,700
Thank you.

445
00:26:58,140 --> 00:26:59,140
Hey, Jane.

446
00:26:59,250 --> 00:27:01,310
It's a light activity for fun,
not a final exam.

447
00:27:01,330 --> 00:27:02,770
Why are you taking it so seriously?

448
00:27:03,390 --> 00:27:05,010
I don't know what to write.

449
00:27:06,820 --> 00:27:08,230
So draw something instead.

450
00:27:11,730 --> 00:27:12,730
What should I draw?

451
00:27:14,540 --> 00:27:15,620
Ah.

452
00:27:15,850 --> 00:27:18,690
So you can draw anything, huh?

453
00:27:20,730 --> 00:27:22,130
Alright.

454
00:27:22,530 --> 00:27:23,930
You're asking for a challenge.

455
00:27:24,440 --> 00:27:25,440
I like that.

456
00:27:25,950 --> 00:27:27,490
Show me what you've got, then.

457
00:27:50,720 --> 00:27:51,720
Whoa!

458
00:27:51,940 --> 00:27:52,940
That's adorable.

459
00:27:53,370 --> 00:27:56,050
You're great at drawing, Jane.

460
00:27:56,740 --> 00:27:57,740
Of course.

461
00:27:57,840 --> 00:28:02,140
I was one of the top
storyboard artists of my class.

462
00:28:02,650 --> 00:28:03,930
Whoa, Jane.

463
00:28:04,220 --> 00:28:06,080
Why haven't you told me
about this before?

464
00:28:06,100 --> 00:28:07,160
Do you know how many times

465
00:28:07,180 --> 00:28:09,850
I've pitched my ideas to the team
with simple stick figures?

466
00:28:10,040 --> 00:28:10,680
Gosh!

467
00:28:11,230 --> 00:28:13,510
It's embarrassing, you know?

468
00:28:13,530 --> 00:28:14,440
Ow.

469
00:28:15,060 --> 00:28:16,310
You've never asked me about it.

470
00:28:17,240 --> 00:28:20,110
I always ask you,
"Is there anything I can help you with?"

471
00:28:20,130 --> 00:28:21,630
But every time you say, "No."

472
00:28:22,570 --> 00:28:24,120
And now you're complaining?

473
00:28:24,870 --> 00:28:26,130
You're right...

474
00:28:26,540 --> 00:28:27,540
Fine.

475
00:28:28,040 --> 00:28:29,040
It's my fault.

476
00:28:29,720 --> 00:28:30,930
I'm sorry!

477
00:28:31,340 --> 00:28:33,040
- Here.
- Please forgive me.

478
00:28:33,450 --> 00:28:34,450
You wanna write anything?

479
00:28:35,760 --> 00:28:36,760
I don't think so.

480
00:28:37,330 --> 00:28:38,810
My handwriting is a mess.

481
00:28:38,930 --> 00:28:40,510
It'll ruin your drawing.

482
00:28:42,030 --> 00:28:43,440
I'll write it for you, then.

483
00:28:43,940 --> 00:28:45,330
What do you want your message to be?

484
00:28:49,430 --> 00:28:50,920
What should it be...?

485
00:28:54,140 --> 00:28:55,730
Oh...

486
00:28:58,930 --> 00:29:00,420
"JaabJane

487
00:29:00,830 --> 00:29:01,830
was here."

488
00:29:02,320 --> 00:29:03,120
How about that?

489
00:29:10,130 --> 00:29:11,540
How about...

490
00:29:11,640 --> 00:29:13,840
"Here, there was JaabJane."

491
00:29:14,730 --> 00:29:15,500
Sounds good?

492
00:30:00,740 --> 00:30:02,530
All done. Let's go.

493
00:30:03,640 --> 00:30:04,450
Huh?

494
00:30:05,430 --> 00:30:06,280
Oh.

495
00:30:06,300 --> 00:30:07,400
Yeah, let's go.

496
00:30:09,540 --> 00:30:10,540
Jane.

497
00:30:11,230 --> 00:30:12,940
Wait... Wait for me.

498
00:30:13,530 --> 00:30:14,530
Jane, Jane.

499
00:30:14,550 --> 00:30:16,740
[May what comes next be wonderful

500
00:30:16,760 --> 00:30:18,480
#JaabJaneWasHere]

501
00:30:19,650 --> 00:30:21,040
Oh. Come on, Sis.

502
00:30:21,060 --> 00:30:23,210
Why is our lead producer so headstrong?

503
00:30:23,230 --> 00:30:24,710
You said the meeting was postponed, no?

504
00:30:24,740 --> 00:30:26,730
Well, it was.

505
00:30:26,850 --> 00:30:28,850
From yesterday to today.

506
00:30:29,030 --> 00:30:31,480
Why didn't you tell me ahead of time?!

507
00:30:31,500 --> 00:30:32,380
I've got an appointment.

508
00:30:32,400 --> 00:30:34,940
I told you I'd have to leave the office early.

509
00:30:35,030 --> 00:30:36,340
Damn it...

510
00:30:37,630 --> 00:30:40,490
Aww. You may leave now, Khanoon.

511
00:30:40,520 --> 00:30:43,060
You can leave right away.
Go ahead.

512
00:30:43,920 --> 00:30:45,530
- Can I?
- Mm.

513
00:30:46,650 --> 00:30:49,390
You can leave, but don't come back again.

514
00:30:49,410 --> 00:30:51,540
Go ahead. Don't come here tomorrow either.

515
00:30:52,940 --> 00:30:55,090
- Ah! Ah!
- Okay?

516
00:30:55,430 --> 00:30:56,940
Please, don't, Sis.

517
00:30:56,960 --> 00:30:58,080
I've learned my lesson, Sis.

518
00:30:58,100 --> 00:30:59,020
Don't say that, please.

519
00:30:59,040 --> 00:31:01,430
Don't hire a new DOP, please.

520
00:31:01,530 --> 00:31:02,430
Ugh!

521
00:31:03,140 --> 00:31:04,120
Jaab, how's it going?

522
00:31:04,140 --> 00:31:05,860
Have you come up with any ideas?

523
00:31:06,030 --> 00:31:08,410
I know that once
the meeting was postponed,

524
00:31:08,430 --> 00:31:10,360
you wouldn't make any progress.

525
00:31:10,380 --> 00:31:11,620
That's what you do.

526
00:31:11,640 --> 00:31:14,320
No deadline, no progress.

527
00:31:14,830 --> 00:31:16,130
Come on, Sis.

528
00:31:16,150 --> 00:31:18,040
I just haven't put my ideas
in the slides.

529
00:31:18,430 --> 00:31:19,730
But I can tell you all about it.

530
00:31:20,220 --> 00:31:21,630
Because I'm...

531
00:31:21,840 --> 00:31:24,160
not as irresponsible as you think.

532
00:31:25,390 --> 00:31:26,240
Mm.

533
00:31:26,340 --> 00:31:30,040
Good. It's great to see some progress.

534
00:31:30,060 --> 00:31:32,390
If changes were to be made,

535
00:31:32,410 --> 00:31:34,050
you could simply
leave the slides untouched.

536
00:31:35,130 --> 00:31:36,150
What do you mean? Changes?

537
00:31:36,240 --> 00:31:38,200
I'll smack you in the mouth.

538
00:31:39,850 --> 00:31:41,440
What an inauspicious thing to say.

539
00:31:41,840 --> 00:31:43,150
I'm very confident

540
00:31:44,020 --> 00:31:45,730
with this draft.

541
00:31:45,940 --> 00:31:48,330
Huh. Are you sure?

542
00:31:48,360 --> 00:31:49,660
It's an MV for a sad song.

543
00:31:49,690 --> 00:31:52,090
I hope it doesn't turn into
a wedding presentation like last time.

544
00:31:54,330 --> 00:31:55,840
Wedding, my ass!

545
00:31:58,930 --> 00:31:59,500
What?

546
00:31:59,580 --> 00:32:01,890
And when did you get that coffee?
You didn't tell me to tag along.

547
00:32:02,710 --> 00:32:03,920
Jane also has one.

548
00:32:03,940 --> 00:32:05,800
You two didn't invite us to come along?

549
00:32:05,820 --> 00:32:07,060
Is there something going on
between you?

550
00:32:12,240 --> 00:32:13,820
Uh...

551
00:32:14,670 --> 00:32:16,000
Pink Team!

552
00:32:16,020 --> 00:32:18,260
Let's... Let's start the meeting!

553
00:32:18,280 --> 00:32:18,710
Shall we?

554
00:32:18,730 --> 00:32:20,080
Come on, Jane.

555
00:32:20,930 --> 00:32:22,360
Come on. Let's move, Jane.

556
00:32:22,640 --> 00:32:24,140
- Hurry up, Jane.
- Oh...

557
00:32:25,720 --> 00:32:27,020
Move, Jane.

558
00:32:27,680 --> 00:32:29,250
See? We work hard.

559
00:32:30,240 --> 00:32:30,890
Look at them...

560
00:32:30,910 --> 00:32:32,420
Hey. Move it, Jane.

561
00:32:39,250 --> 00:32:40,440
Really?

562
00:32:40,830 --> 00:32:41,900
Right?

563
00:32:42,550 --> 00:32:43,500
No wonder...

564
00:32:43,520 --> 00:32:44,520
I can sense it.

565
00:32:51,630 --> 00:32:52,630
Uh...

566
00:32:52,900 --> 00:32:53,900
Pun.

567
00:32:54,340 --> 00:32:54,710
Yes?

568
00:32:54,730 --> 00:32:57,290
Why "Pink Team"?

569
00:33:03,540 --> 00:33:05,520
It's a superstition.

570
00:33:05,830 --> 00:33:07,150
Like, spooky stuff.

571
00:33:07,340 --> 00:33:08,170
Huh?

572
00:33:08,950 --> 00:33:10,940
Well... Position-wise,

573
00:33:11,130 --> 00:33:13,080
Bew has the most power, right?

574
00:33:14,610 --> 00:33:17,520
But to get ideas approved easily
and to diminish some of her authority,

575
00:33:17,930 --> 00:33:19,340
we agreed to name our group

576
00:33:19,640 --> 00:33:21,340
after the meaning of
Chomphoo's name

577
00:33:21,620 --> 00:33:23,050
to undermine Bew's power.

578
00:33:23,450 --> 00:33:24,450
Is that true?

579
00:33:24,730 --> 00:33:25,690
Nope.

580
00:33:26,800 --> 00:33:28,020
Oh...

581
00:33:28,530 --> 00:33:30,320
I actually believed that.

582
00:33:30,730 --> 00:33:31,410
Well...

583
00:33:31,930 --> 00:33:33,320
During the New Year's party,

584
00:33:33,720 --> 00:33:36,220
we had to name our team
for the lucky draw.

585
00:33:37,320 --> 00:33:39,450
We had to come up with a name
when we were already drunk.

586
00:33:39,740 --> 00:33:41,120
So Jaab just blurted out a name.

587
00:33:42,340 --> 00:33:45,250
The color pink is pretty cutesy,

588
00:33:45,610 --> 00:33:47,430
and it suits our team.

589
00:33:51,420 --> 00:33:52,260
Oh...

590
00:33:53,530 --> 00:33:54,530
Not cutesy?

591
00:33:59,330 --> 00:34:00,730
Uh, Pun.

592
00:34:00,750 --> 00:34:01,420
Hm?

593
00:34:01,930 --> 00:34:03,740
About Jaab and Jane,

594
00:34:03,760 --> 00:34:04,240
I...

595
00:34:07,850 --> 00:34:09,350
Never speak about this.

596
00:34:10,040 --> 00:34:12,040
But Jane already...

597
00:34:12,240 --> 00:34:13,830
I told you. Don't bring it up.

598
00:34:14,850 --> 00:34:15,850
Let's get to the meeting.

599
00:34:17,930 --> 00:34:18,760
Come on.

600
00:34:32,230 --> 00:34:34,140
I think your ideas sound alright.

601
00:34:34,840 --> 00:34:36,070
I agree, Sis.

602
00:34:36,330 --> 00:34:37,670
Going through the past moments

603
00:34:37,690 --> 00:34:39,010
should devastate the viewers.

604
00:34:39,080 --> 00:34:40,370
Right?!

605
00:34:40,840 --> 00:34:42,410
That's what I'm aiming for.

606
00:34:43,430 --> 00:34:46,220
And when do you think it'll be ready, Jaab?

607
00:34:46,440 --> 00:34:48,380
I'll schedule the deadline with the client.

608
00:34:48,810 --> 00:34:49,810
Mm...

609
00:34:49,830 --> 00:34:50,930
I think...

610
00:34:50,950 --> 00:34:52,970
it should be ready in a few days.

611
00:34:52,990 --> 00:34:53,930
Mm.

612
00:34:54,100 --> 00:34:55,640
How about we schedule a date for scouting?

613
00:34:56,030 --> 00:34:57,400
We should include actual images, too.

614
00:34:57,420 --> 00:34:59,340
So the client will get
a clearer picture. Okay?

615
00:34:59,440 --> 00:35:02,020
Also, I want you all to finalize
all of the ideas.

616
00:35:02,040 --> 00:35:05,330
So I can request the first draw
from the budget to keep our cash flow going.

617
00:35:06,340 --> 00:35:07,510
How about the day after tomorrow?

618
00:35:07,530 --> 00:35:08,770
Everyone's free, right?

619
00:35:09,660 --> 00:35:10,470
Mm, yeah.

620
00:35:10,840 --> 00:35:12,970
Do you want a van? I'll contact one.

621
00:35:13,240 --> 00:35:14,240
What do you think?

622
00:35:14,260 --> 00:35:16,700
Or do you want the gas money?

623
00:35:16,840 --> 00:35:18,220
Gas money sounds better.

624
00:35:18,240 --> 00:35:19,980
- So I can scoot when it's a wrap.
- Mm.

625
00:35:20,040 --> 00:35:21,040
Agreed.

626
00:35:21,150 --> 00:35:24,130
I don't feel like driving back
into the city, Sis.

627
00:35:25,140 --> 00:35:26,880
Okay, so that settles it.

628
00:35:26,900 --> 00:35:28,250
And... Ai,

629
00:35:28,270 --> 00:35:29,400
you're coming with the team.

630
00:35:29,420 --> 00:35:30,320
Go help Jane.

631
00:35:30,630 --> 00:35:31,890
Okay, sure.

632
00:35:32,440 --> 00:35:33,280
Anything else?

633
00:35:33,300 --> 00:35:34,050
I don't think so.

634
00:35:34,940 --> 00:35:36,060
- Nobody wants to bring up anything?
- No.

635
00:35:36,080 --> 00:35:37,390
Right. We're all done here.

636
00:35:37,410 --> 00:35:39,090
- I'm fine with anything.
- Okay.

637
00:35:39,110 --> 00:35:41,230
- Hey...
- That's about it. Right, Sis?

638
00:35:54,710 --> 00:35:56,500
Are you two a couple?

639
00:35:57,340 --> 00:35:58,340
No.

640
00:35:58,630 --> 00:35:59,700
What makes you say that?

641
00:36:01,070 --> 00:36:02,410
I'm sorry.

642
00:36:02,430 --> 00:36:05,220
Uh... You two seem very close.

643
00:36:07,330 --> 00:36:08,950
Jaab and I are friends.

644
00:36:09,420 --> 00:36:11,570
He's my close friend.

645
00:36:16,050 --> 00:36:17,640
I'm actually

646
00:36:17,930 --> 00:36:20,040
interested in someone already.

647
00:36:29,780 --> 00:36:30,500
Jane!

648
00:36:30,650 --> 00:36:32,540
Look out! A shark!

649
00:36:34,640 --> 00:36:36,000
- Gosh, Jaab. Who's going to...
- Nom, nom, nom.

650
00:36:36,020 --> 00:36:36,910
- Yeah. Take that, you shark.
- Ow, Jane!

651
00:36:36,930 --> 00:36:37,640
Jane, Jane, Jane.

652
00:36:37,660 --> 00:36:38,550
Jane! Jane! Jane!

653
00:36:38,570 --> 00:36:39,910
Ow! I'm sorry!

654
00:36:43,240 --> 00:36:45,970
Ai, do you think
Jaab can win Jane's heart?

655
00:36:48,230 --> 00:36:49,470
Win his heart?

656
00:36:49,860 --> 00:36:50,800
Mm.

657
00:36:51,280 --> 00:36:52,930
It looks possible, though.

658
00:36:52,950 --> 00:36:55,660
Jane is closer to Jaab than
anyone else in the office.

659
00:36:56,440 --> 00:36:59,140
And they get along very well
in so many aspects.

660
00:36:59,160 --> 00:37:00,230
Don't you think so?

661
00:37:00,920 --> 00:37:01,780
Pun.

662
00:37:02,420 --> 00:37:03,490
Mm.

663
00:37:03,650 --> 00:37:06,150
Uh... About Jaab and Jane,

664
00:37:06,690 --> 00:37:09,810
I don't think that's how it goes.

665
00:37:30,730 --> 00:37:31,620
Oh... Oh.

666
00:37:38,500 --> 00:37:40,600
Not only are you not helping,

667
00:37:40,810 --> 00:37:42,330
but you're also distracting me, Jaab.

668
00:37:42,800 --> 00:37:44,590
This is your own work, too.

669
00:37:45,200 --> 00:37:46,420
What?

670
00:37:46,600 --> 00:37:48,200
You said you wanted to help.

671
00:37:48,220 --> 00:37:49,820
Well, I'm letting you help me.

672
00:37:51,500 --> 00:37:53,460
This isn't "letting me help."

673
00:37:53,600 --> 00:37:55,520
This is "dumping your work on me."

674
00:38:02,190 --> 00:38:02,910
Well...

675
00:38:03,720 --> 00:38:05,660
I don't know how to help you.

676
00:38:05,910 --> 00:38:07,300
If I drew something,

677
00:38:07,320 --> 00:38:09,180
the work would end up
like that one horse meme.

678
00:38:10,900 --> 00:38:11,810
What horse meme?

679
00:38:11,830 --> 00:38:12,610
Huh?

680
00:38:12,630 --> 00:38:14,420
You haven't seen it?

681
00:38:14,440 --> 00:38:15,500
The horse drawing meme.

682
00:38:15,520 --> 00:38:18,170
The body of the horse is
beautifully sketched.

683
00:38:18,190 --> 00:38:19,690
But its head

684
00:38:19,710 --> 00:38:20,870
looks sloppy like...

685
00:38:20,890 --> 00:38:22,690
it was drawn by a kindergartener.

686
00:38:39,530 --> 00:38:40,110
How's that?

687
00:38:40,540 --> 00:38:41,330
Uh...

688
00:38:42,100 --> 00:38:43,100
Hold on, Jaab.

689
00:38:43,120 --> 00:38:44,750
What are you doing?

690
00:38:45,100 --> 00:38:47,190
Oh, I'm giving you a massage.

691
00:38:47,210 --> 00:38:48,250
In case your arm is tired.

692
00:38:48,710 --> 00:38:49,490
Okay?

693
00:38:50,320 --> 00:38:51,910
But you're moving my arm.

694
00:38:52,900 --> 00:38:54,490
The lines are all messy now.

695
00:38:55,200 --> 00:38:56,200
Oh...

696
00:39:02,370 --> 00:39:04,510
I can't do anything.

697
00:39:05,300 --> 00:39:06,300
Ugh...

698
00:39:06,900 --> 00:39:08,140
How the hell am I supposed to help?

699
00:39:21,830 --> 00:39:22,590
Jane!

700
00:39:23,200 --> 00:39:23,910
Hm?

701
00:39:24,920 --> 00:39:25,920
Jane!

702
00:39:27,990 --> 00:39:28,890
What is it, Jaab?

703
00:39:29,360 --> 00:39:30,920
Three... Four...

704
00:39:30,950 --> 00:39:33,310
♫Let's go, Jane, you've got this♫

705
00:39:33,330 --> 00:39:34,780
♫Let's go, Jane, you can do it♫

706
00:39:34,800 --> 00:39:36,760
- ♫Let's go♫
- Wait, wait, wait.

707
00:39:37,200 --> 00:39:38,200
What are you doing?

708
00:39:39,010 --> 00:39:40,090
I'm cheering you on, obviously.

709
00:39:40,110 --> 00:39:42,450
♫Let's go, Jane, you've got this♫

710
00:39:42,470 --> 00:39:44,500
♫Let's go, Jane, you can do it♫

711
00:39:44,650 --> 00:39:46,830
♫Let's go, Jane, you've got this♫

712
00:39:46,850 --> 00:39:48,990
♫Let's go, Jane, you can do it♫

713
00:39:49,010 --> 00:39:50,380
♫Let's go, Jane♫

714
00:40:57,900 --> 00:40:58,900
Jane...

715
00:41:01,200 --> 00:41:03,540
How about you continue
the work tomorrow?

716
00:41:05,110 --> 00:41:06,620
I was about to wake you up.

717
00:41:06,920 --> 00:41:07,920
I wanted to tell you that...

718
00:41:08,430 --> 00:41:09,060
it's all done.

719
00:41:10,410 --> 00:41:11,410
Really?

720
00:41:19,510 --> 00:41:20,280
Here.

721
00:41:24,100 --> 00:41:25,360
I'm sorry, Jane.

722
00:41:26,490 --> 00:41:27,820
I feel really bad now.

723
00:41:28,000 --> 00:41:29,530
I didn't think that
it would take this long.

724
00:41:29,720 --> 00:41:30,590
If I had known,

725
00:41:30,840 --> 00:41:33,100
I would've stuck to the stick figures.

726
00:41:35,300 --> 00:41:36,840
You're only starting to feel bad

727
00:41:36,860 --> 00:41:38,740
now that the work is done?

728
00:41:48,400 --> 00:41:49,150
And...

729
00:41:49,590 --> 00:41:50,800
what now, Jane?

730
00:41:51,010 --> 00:41:52,810
Are you heading home? Or...

731
00:41:52,910 --> 00:41:54,630
do you want to have
a late dinner with me?

732
00:41:54,690 --> 00:41:56,420
It's my treat.

733
00:41:57,320 --> 00:41:58,900
Um...

734
00:41:58,920 --> 00:42:00,200
I'm heading home, probably.

735
00:42:00,890 --> 00:42:02,200
Oh, I see.

736
00:42:02,610 --> 00:42:03,610
Mm.

737
00:42:03,720 --> 00:42:04,510
Okay.

738
00:42:04,800 --> 00:42:05,560
Let's just say...

739
00:42:05,580 --> 00:42:07,580
I owe you a meal.

740
00:42:09,430 --> 00:42:10,620
- Okay?
- Mm.

741
00:42:16,810 --> 00:42:17,810
What's so funny, Jane?

742
00:42:18,120 --> 00:42:18,990
Hm?

743
00:42:19,710 --> 00:42:21,440
I'm handsome, I know.
But don't stare too often.

744
00:42:22,210 --> 00:42:23,490
Do you have a pet bird or what?

745
00:42:25,700 --> 00:42:26,700
I don't.

746
00:42:28,400 --> 00:42:29,290
See?

747
00:42:29,310 --> 00:42:31,110
Your hair looks like a bird's nest.

748
00:42:51,790 --> 00:42:52,790
Mm.

749
00:42:53,320 --> 00:42:55,790
Well, let me go grab my stuff.

750
00:42:57,420 --> 00:42:58,420
Right.

751
00:43:09,800 --> 00:43:10,800
Jane!

752
00:43:10,820 --> 00:43:12,920
My hair's messy again, Jane.

753
00:43:12,940 --> 00:43:15,190
Ow! There's a whole flock
on my head, Jane!

754
00:43:15,220 --> 00:43:16,980
Help me fix it, please...

755
00:43:17,010 --> 00:43:17,740
Jane!

756
00:43:18,350 --> 00:43:19,600
Jane, wait up!

757
00:43:31,200 --> 00:43:32,020
What are you doing?

758
00:43:32,040 --> 00:43:32,990
Listening to some music?

759
00:43:33,320 --> 00:43:34,820
Oh, yeah.

760
00:43:34,840 --> 00:43:37,510
I want to recheck it quickly before
sending the storyboard to the group chat.

761
00:43:40,000 --> 00:43:41,000
Do you want to...

762
00:43:41,310 --> 00:43:42,140
listen with me?

763
00:43:42,890 --> 00:43:43,550
Mm.

764
00:43:45,850 --> 00:43:47,150
Okay. Here.

765
00:44:04,660 --> 00:44:05,230
Uh... Jane.

766
00:44:05,900 --> 00:44:06,600
Hm?

767
00:44:08,620 --> 00:44:09,990
About our movie plan,

768
00:44:10,300 --> 00:44:12,700
there's a theater near Sukhumvit.

769
00:44:12,720 --> 00:44:14,260
- It's called...
- Oh, is it "3sept"?

770
00:44:14,380 --> 00:44:15,100
What?!

771
00:44:15,300 --> 00:44:16,150
You know it?!

772
00:44:16,310 --> 00:44:17,060
Of course.

773
00:44:17,950 --> 00:44:19,500
I always went there
back in my university days.

774
00:44:19,520 --> 00:44:22,940
It's peaceful there.
So many good films, too.

775
00:44:23,020 --> 00:44:24,020
Whoa...

776
00:44:24,400 --> 00:44:25,240
You have great taste.

777
00:44:26,330 --> 00:44:28,340
So you like niche films, too?

778
00:44:28,700 --> 00:44:30,390
I used to go there with Min all the time.

779
00:44:31,240 --> 00:44:32,490
But after graduation,

780
00:44:32,510 --> 00:44:34,430
we parted ways for our jobs.

781
00:44:34,610 --> 00:44:35,780
So I completely forgot about it.

782
00:44:36,770 --> 00:44:37,740
- Right...
- Oh.

783
00:44:38,310 --> 00:44:39,310
Now that I'm talking about it...

784
00:44:39,330 --> 00:44:41,110
I feel kinda nostalgic.

785
00:44:44,290 --> 00:44:45,290
How about...

786
00:44:46,420 --> 00:44:48,610
we go there sometime?

787
00:44:49,610 --> 00:44:50,380
Sure.

788
00:44:50,920 --> 00:44:51,820
Really?

789
00:45:01,100 --> 00:45:02,100
By the way,

790
00:45:02,120 --> 00:45:03,220
both of us...

791
00:45:03,490 --> 00:45:05,300
have so much in common, don't we?

792
00:45:07,020 --> 00:45:10,630
At a glance, it might seem like
we wouldn't get along,

793
00:45:10,980 --> 00:45:11,980
but...

794
00:45:12,510 --> 00:45:14,510
we've got so much in common.

795
00:45:14,910 --> 00:45:15,910
Both of us.

796
00:45:18,110 --> 00:45:19,120
Agreed.

797
00:45:21,220 --> 00:45:22,220
And...

798
00:45:22,600 --> 00:45:25,110
do you believe in the chemistry
between two people?

799
00:45:29,500 --> 00:45:30,950
Chemistry?

800
00:45:31,190 --> 00:45:32,270
Mm.

801
00:45:32,900 --> 00:45:34,400
Like the chemistry...

802
00:45:34,710 --> 00:45:37,110
between two characters?

803
00:45:39,320 --> 00:45:40,320
Exactly.

804
00:45:44,060 --> 00:45:45,010
Right...

805
00:46:07,700 --> 00:46:08,700
- Jane.
- Hm?

806
00:46:08,910 --> 00:46:10,970
Whose phone should we use
to call for a ride?

807
00:46:11,910 --> 00:46:12,800
It's fine.

808
00:46:12,820 --> 00:46:14,190
Someone's picking me up.

809
00:46:14,510 --> 00:46:15,590
You wanna tag along?

810
00:46:16,100 --> 00:46:18,500
I might bring a friend with me,
I mentioned that.

811
00:46:19,220 --> 00:46:20,220
Whoa...

812
00:46:20,680 --> 00:46:22,020
Who is it?

813
00:46:22,040 --> 00:46:23,300
Is it your family?

814
00:46:23,590 --> 00:46:24,340
Or is it Min?

815
00:46:26,410 --> 00:46:27,410
His name is Mon.

816
00:46:32,600 --> 00:46:33,550
Mon?

817
00:46:35,420 --> 00:46:36,600
I've been talking to him.

818
00:46:45,510 --> 00:46:46,680
You've been talking?

819
00:46:47,390 --> 00:46:48,380
Mm.

820
00:46:54,280 --> 00:46:55,900
There he is. Perfect timing.

821
00:47:20,600 --> 00:47:21,780
Did I keep you waiting?

822
00:47:22,010 --> 00:47:23,380
I came as quickly as I could.

823
00:47:23,900 --> 00:47:26,030
Not at all. We're just here, too.

824
00:47:28,520 --> 00:47:29,520
Jaab, right?

825
00:47:30,600 --> 00:47:32,000
You're tagging along with us, yeah?

826
00:47:32,290 --> 00:47:33,600
Jane told me about you.

827
00:47:42,410 --> 00:47:43,410
Oh...

828
00:47:44,600 --> 00:47:46,250
I don't want to be trouble.

829
00:47:46,800 --> 00:47:48,120
What? Why?

830
00:47:50,090 --> 00:47:51,680
Uh... Well,

831
00:47:51,700 --> 00:47:53,510
my mom just texted me

832
00:47:53,720 --> 00:47:54,900
to come home right away.

833
00:47:55,900 --> 00:47:56,900
Oh, really?

834
00:47:58,200 --> 00:47:59,200
I guess...

835
00:48:00,220 --> 00:48:01,220
this is where we call it, then?

836
00:48:01,800 --> 00:48:02,800
Mm.

837
00:48:04,220 --> 00:48:05,220
Mon,

838
00:48:06,730 --> 00:48:07,340
have a good one.

839
00:48:07,360 --> 00:48:08,410
You, too.

840
00:48:24,710 --> 00:48:25,710
Wait, Jaab.

841
00:48:43,400 --> 00:48:44,800
You forgot to give this back
to your friend?

842
00:48:45,900 --> 00:48:47,450
Oh, right.

843
00:49:14,210 --> 00:49:15,900
Jane told me so much about you.

844
00:49:17,010 --> 00:49:18,010
Thank you

845
00:49:18,900 --> 00:49:20,100
for being his close friend.

846
00:49:23,710 --> 00:49:24,710
It's my pleasure.

847
00:49:26,910 --> 00:49:27,910
Should we get going?

848
00:49:29,220 --> 00:49:30,220
Bye-bye, Jaab.

849
00:49:30,620 --> 00:49:31,810
See you, Jane.

850
00:50:20,410 --> 00:50:21,410
Hello, Mek.

851
00:50:27,900 --> 00:50:28,900
Damn it...

852
00:50:29,810 --> 00:50:31,490
I'm not the one...

853
00:50:32,870 --> 00:50:34,640
Mek, I'm not the one.

854
00:50:34,940 --> 00:50:36,310
I've been imagining it on my own.

855
00:50:37,000 --> 00:50:38,590
I've been imagining it from the start!

856
00:50:42,890 --> 00:50:45,390
Chemistry is the connection between characters.

857
00:50:45,410 --> 00:50:47,690
It's a feeling that lights up

858
00:50:47,910 --> 00:50:49,900
when two people are together.

859
00:50:50,100 --> 00:50:53,000
Chemistry turns ordinary scenes
into special ones.

860
00:50:54,510 --> 00:50:57,200
It happens on its own

861
00:50:57,410 --> 00:50:58,800
without an explanation.

862
00:50:59,110 --> 00:51:00,190
It's not an exact science.

863
00:51:00,500 --> 00:51:01,900
No rules set in stone.

864
00:51:02,520 --> 00:51:04,080
It's like an eruption in my heart

865
00:51:05,300 --> 00:51:07,220
that I've been imagining...

866
00:51:07,700 --> 00:51:08,920
all on my own.

867
00:51:31,010 --> 00:51:33,200
Shit... My heart is broken.

868
00:51:33,300 --> 00:51:34,460
Broken, my ass.

869
00:51:34,480 --> 00:51:35,480
You two were never even a thing.

870
00:51:35,890 --> 00:51:36,920
That guy is just someone Jane's talking to.

871
00:51:37,010 --> 00:51:38,550
They're not official yet.
You have a chance, no?

872
00:51:38,570 --> 00:51:39,920
I'll lose either way.

873
00:51:40,050 --> 00:51:41,210
Wouldn't it be better...

874
00:51:41,240 --> 00:51:43,400
if I stayed like this so that
Jane would still be around?

875
00:51:43,720 --> 00:51:45,080
What should I do, Jane?

876
00:51:45,280 --> 00:51:46,440
I'm...

877
00:51:46,490 --> 00:51:47,870
so fucking in love with you.

878
00:51:48,920 --> 00:51:49,900
Before I can...
[I'm sorry]

879
00:51:49,920 --> 00:51:51,560
call somebody "a friend,"

880
00:51:51,710 --> 00:51:53,400
it's really hard for me, Jaab.
